# [[o]] {{şerh|bir eşitlik cümlesini veya bir fiil cümlesini sunar<!--introduces an equational clause or a verb phrase-->}}
#: {{ux|ar|هَلْ تَعْلَمُ '''أَنَّ'''نِي أَطْوَلُ مِنْكَ؟|Senden boylu old'''uğumu''' bilir misin?}}
#: {{ux|ar|أَعْرِفُ '''أَنَّ''' ٱبْنَكَ سَرَقَ سَيَّارَتِي.|Oğlunun otomobilimi çald'''ığını''' biliyorum.}}
<!--
=====Açıklamalar=====
* If pertaining to a verb, {{m-self|ar|أَنَّ}} and the clause it introduces are syntactically its ''object''. This distinguishes {{m-self|ar|أَنَّ}} from {{m-self|ar|أَنْ}}, especially in the case outlined in the usage note above.
* {{m-self|ar|أَنَّ}} must be followed immediately by the subject of the clause it introduces, in the accusative case. An attached object pronoun can satisfy this condition.
** The sole exception is in the relevant sense of {{m-self|ar|أَنْ}} above. In that case, such a subject ''can'' appear and cause the {{m-self|ar|أَنَّ}} pronunciation to resurface, but it is only optional. Compare the following alternative phrasing: {{misal|ar|أَشْهَدُ '''أَنَّهُ''' لَا إِلٰهَ إِلَّا اللَّهُ|t=I bear witness '''that''' there is no god but God.}}-->

